{% set intro %}
    <p>Invented by John F. Byrne in the 1920s. Only someone with the same settings can decode a message. For example, <code class="tool-example">Hello World</code> becomes <code class="tool-example">Wahqz Iuets</code>. Spaces, punctuation and numbers pass through unchanged.</p>
    <p>More on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaocipher" class="text-convrtr">Chaocipher</a> Wikipedia page.</p>
